speechtext:
Mr. Chairman, the Minister of Transport complained the other day in another debate that I took part in debates on what were described as trivial matters and had nothing to say about the important declaration he made recently on shipping. So as to relieve the minister of his disappointment in the matter, I intend to say something about his announcement and I wish to say how much I welcomed these words uttered by the minister the other day, as found on page 4783 of Hansard. With respect to his statement he said;
We intend to help the fishermen who are working in very small boats. We are going to look after them, too.
That is a promise that will be welcomed by all the fishermen on the Atlantic coast. It was, of course, what was asked for by the hon. member for Grand Falls-White Bay-Labrador the other day in committee of supply on the estimates of one of the minister's colleagues, and we were rather disappointed when it was found that fishermen in small boats were not included in the declaration the minister made the other day with respect to aid for fishermen in the larger boats.
